'''Rangas''' ({{Audio|OpenSpeaks-kfy-Johari-Surendra Singh Pangtey Rangkas.wav|pronunciation}}) or '''Rangkas''' is an extinct [[West Himalayish languages|West Himalayish language]] spoken by the Rangkas people of [[Uttarakhand]], [[India]]. The Rangkas joined the [[Kumaoni people]] and shifted to [[Kumaoni language|their language]]. There is currently an ethnic population of about 1,000 people.

Rangas was spoken in [[Dharchula]] and [[Munsiyari]] tehsils (facing the Nepal border along the Mahakali valley), [[Johar Valley]], [[Pithoragarh District]], [[Uttarakhand]], [[India]].<ref name=e18>[http://www.ethnologue.com/language/rgk Ethnologue entry for Rangas]</ref>

